SOLUTION: Applied surgical patches to three files and ran the deployer: (1) Patched gfxPlatformGtk.cpp::InitPlatformGPUProcessPrefs() to comment out the Wayland GPU process ForceDisable block, restoring GPU process startup on Wayland. This enables VA-API decode in RDD process + zero-copy DMABUF import via GPU process to compositor. (2) Uncommented AudioContext.cpp and AudioDestinationNode.cpp deploy lines in deploy.sh, deploying 48kHz native sample rate enforcement and Fast-Tanh soft clipper in DestinationNodeEngine::ProcessBlock. (3) Ran ./deploy.sh which successfully copied all 396 patch files to /home/gorilla/firefox-source/. Verified deployed source contains: GPU process unblock, VA-API decode sanity-test dead-code (false &&), codec blocklist (VP8/VP9/AV1/HEVC blocked, H.264 forced), vendor override (0x8086/0x1002/0x10de), UDP send buffer 4194304, NEGATIVE_RECORD_LIFETIME=3, upload pacing constant wired in nsHttpTransaction.cpp.

Key technical details:

**GPU Process Unblock (gfxPlatformGtk.cpp lines 326-335):**
- Original code unconditionally called gpuProc.ForceDisable(Blocked, "Wayland does not work in the GPU process", FEATURE_FAILURE_WAYLAND) when IsWaylandDisplay() returned true.
- Patch comments out the entire block with GORILLA prefix comment. This allows GPU process to start on Wayland.
- Downstream effect: HW_DECODED_VIDEO_ZERO_COPY (blocklisted in about:support line 295) becomes available because GPU process exists to receive DMABUF frames from RDD.
- RDD process VA-API decode was already working (H264_HW_DECODE shows "available" in decision log), but frames had to copy through CPU memory without GPU process.

**Audio Patches Deployed:**
- AudioContext.cpp: GetSampleRateForAudioContext() now returns 48000.0f when media.gorilla.hardware_only_mode pref is true, bypassing CubebUtils::PreferredSampleRate(). OutputLatency() Linux fallback reduced from 25ms to 10ms for PipeWire alignment.
- AudioDestinationNode.cpp: DestinationNodeEngine::ProcessBlock() now allocates writable channels via AllocateChannels(), copies input scaled by volume, applies Fast-Tanh soft clipper (x * (27 + x^2) / (27 + 9x^2)) per sample, sets mVolume=1.0f since gain is baked into samples. Guarded by StaticPrefs::media_gorilla_hardware_only_mode().

**Networking Patches Verified Deployed:**
- HttpConnectionUDP.cpp:333 mSocket->SetSendBufferSize(4194304) // 4MB
- nsHostResolver.cpp:74 NEGATIVE_RECORD_LIFETIME = 3 (was 60)
- nsHttpTransaction.cpp:867-869 kGorillaUploadChunkSize (256KB) pacing in ReadSegments() for large uploads
- All telemetry gated by #ifndef GLEAN_DISABLED (GLEAN_DISABLED=1 defined in patched files)

**Codec Blocklist (GfxInfo.cpp lines 1481-1495):**
- FEATURE_H264_HW_DECODE/ENCODE -> FEATURE_STATUS_OK
- VP8/VP9/AV1/HEVC -> FEATURE_BLOCKED_PLATFORM_TEST with FEATURE_FAILURE_GORILLA_NO_HW_CODEC

**Vendor Override (GfxInfoBase.cpp 1127-1132, GfxInfo.cpp 1477-1495):**
- Checks for "0x8086" (Intel), "0x1002" (AMD), "0x10de" (NVIDIA) -> FEATURE_STATUS_OK bypassing blocklist

**Sanity Test Dead-Code (gfxPlatform.cpp 3065, 3117):**
- media.hardware-video-decoding.failed and media.hardware-video-encoding.failed prefs wrapped in `false &&` so one bad boot never permanently disables VA-API/QuickSync.

CODE:
// gfxPlatformGtk.cpp - GPU Process Wayland Unblock
